# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) only if you need to change a default.
#
# Where `npm run dev` forwards /api. The default is the Node API from the
# sibling Backend/ directory on its own default port.
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:37411

# Where the built app sends its requests. Unset means same-origin `/api`,
# which is what the dev proxy provides and what a deployment behind one
# reverse proxy provides too. Leaving it unset is also what keeps one built
# bundle working on localhost, staging and production without a rebuild: no
# address is compiled into it, and the browser resolves /api against whatever
# origin served the page.
#
# Set it only when the API really is on another origin — and then that origin
# has to be on the backend's TOOLTRACK_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, or the browser will
# drop the session cookie.
#
# That allowlist is necessary and not sufficient. The session cookie is
# SameSite=Lax, which is about the site rather than the origin: app.example.com
# calling api.example.com works, and app.example.com calling api.elsewhere.com
# does not — CORS lets the answer through, the browser sends no cookie, and
# every call arrives anonymous. Backend/README.md says what changing that would
# cost.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/api
